WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.603
Practice is necessary for expertise, but not all practice has the same value.

2
00:00:05.603 --> 00:00:10.776
Repeating a comfortable task can maintain familiarity without building much new capability.

3
00:00:10.776 --> 00:00:12.931
Deliberate practice is more focused.

4
00:00:12.931 --> 00:00:17.672
It uses clear goals, concentrated effort, feedback, correction, and increasing challenge.

5
00:00:17.672 --> 00:00:26.724
It asks the learner to work at the edge of current ability, where improvement is possible but mistakes are still visible.

6
00:00:26.724 --> 00:00:30.603
Complex skills often need to be broken into components.

7
00:00:30.603 --> 00:00:38.792
A skilled analyst, engineer, operator, or manager performs many small judgments that are easy to miss from the outside.

8
00:00:38.792 --> 00:00:49.137
Training can isolate those components: recognizing cues, choosing a method, checking an assumption, explaining a tradeoff, reviewing an output, or recovering from an error.

9
00:00:49.137 --> 00:00:54.309
Once the components improve, they can be recombined into more realistic performance.

10
00:00:54.309 --> 00:00:57.326
Time served does not automatically produce expertise.

11
00:00:57.326 --> 00:01:09.395
Someone can repeat the same weak approach for years if the environment never provides clear feedback or if mistakes are hidden by luck, team support, or forgiving conditions.

12
00:01:09.395 --> 00:01:19.309
Experience becomes more valuable when it includes reflection, correction, increasing complexity, and enough variation to teach when the old pattern no longer applies.

13
00:01:19.309 --> 00:01:25.774
A useful improvement cycle is simple to describe, even when it takes discipline to execute.

14
00:01:25.774 --> 00:01:27.498
Define the target performance.

15
00:01:27.498 --> 00:01:28.791
Attempt the task.

16
00:01:28.791 --> 00:01:31.808
Compare the result against a stronger standard.

17
00:01:31.808 --> 00:01:33.101
Identify the gap.

18
00:01:33.101 --> 00:01:34.394
Adjust the method.

19
00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:37.412
Try again under a slightly different condition.

20
00:01:37.412 --> 00:01:43.877
Expertise grows through many cycles like this, not through a single heroic burst of effort.
